# One author in the graph, one identity in history.
#
# GitLab attributes a commit to a user by its email address. This history grew
# through three identities — the GitHub noreply (129 commits), plus "Timman6866"
# and "tinMan" (7 commits between them) — none of which is the address on the
# GitLab account, so every commit showed as an unattributed author.
#
# Canonical form is <proper name> <proper email> <commit name> <commit email>.
# The name stays MRsmallAgain because that is what 129 of the 136 commits say;
# the email is the account address, which is what actually drives attribution.
MRsmallAgain <ozzman6866@gmail.com> MRsmallAgain <MRsmallAgain@users.noreply.github.com>
MRsmallAgain <ozzman6866@gmail.com> Timman6866 <ozzman6866@gmail.com>
MRsmallAgain <ozzman6866@gmail.com> tinMan <ozzman6866@gmail.com>
